sk6502 (ISC)
  The Commodore 64 BASIC and KERNAL labels and descriptions in
  src/decompnet/rom/c64_rommap.py come from sk6502's c64rom.ctl
  (https://github.com/skoolkid/sk6502), Copyright 2019 Richard Dymond.
  The ISC copyright and permission notice is in that module's header and in
  licenses/sk6502-ISC.txt.

  That control file states that its annotations are derived from
  "The almost completely commented C64 ROM disassembly", V1.01, by Lee Davison,
  2012. Davison's original disassembly carries no explicit open-source licence.
  The ISC notice covers Richard Dymond's sk6502 distribution, which is the copy
  this project vendors. I/O, colour RAM, screen RAM and the usual zero-page
  names in src/decompnet/rom/c64_hw.py are not from sk6502.
